From 87a867a8f924edce495cf54b619bdef44ac6954f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SplitMind <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:41:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gmail): download attachments on non-streaming transit
 backends

download_attachment refused every transit backend without createFromStream,
so on Cloudflare Workers (KV or R2 transit files) Gmail attachments could not
be fetched at all.

Without createFromStream, read the response with the usual byte bound
(4/3 of the transit limit plus the envelope allowance), parse it with
JSON.parse, decode the base64url data with Buffer and hand the bytes to
create(). The same checks as the streaming parser apply: valid base64url,
declared size matches, transit limit (413). Native decoding also costs about
20x less CPU than the character-level streaming parser (about 4.5 ms vs
100 ms per MiB on Node), which matters under Workers CPU limits.

Streaming backends (filesystem) keep the bounded-memory path unchanged.
